      "text": "Let \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) be the two numbers such that \\( x > y \\). Given the conditions:\n\n1. The sum of the two numbers is 6:\n   \\[\n   x + y = 6\n   \\]\n\n2. The difference of their squares is 12:\n   \\[\n   x^2 - y^2 = 12\n   \\]\n\nWe can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\( x^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y) \\). Substituting the given sum into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n(x + y)(x - y) = 12\n\\]\nSubstituting \\( x + y = 6 \\) into the equation, we have:\n\\[\n6(x - y) = 12\n\\]\nSolving for \\( x - y \\), we divide both sides by 6:\n\\[\nx - y = \\frac{12}{6} = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the positive difference of the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
